                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Extract from the Critic, August 6,
                        1881.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">from the mexican capital.—war of extermination
                        against indian depredators.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >City of Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi>
                        6</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>General Boquet has left the city for Chihuahua to assume command of the troops in
                    that district. His orders from the government are understood to be to collect
                    and combine such of the scattered forces of that State as can be got quickly
                    together and carry on a war of extermination against Indian marauders who have
                    crossed the border, and who are reported as devastating the country.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
